<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwSA" aria-labelledby="Remark_on_filtrations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Remark_on_filtrations">Remark on filtrations</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Remark on filtrations"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwSQ">Note that similar to Hodge structures, mixed Hodge structures use a filtration instead of a direct sum decomposition since the cohomology groups with anti-holomorphic terms, <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt30" id="mwSg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{p,q}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{p,q}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>p</mi>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mi>q</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{p,q}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/fb00ccee8c508c8c48f7948cf82cdcc53c801fb8" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.376ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{p,q}}"/></span> where <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt31" id="mwSw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"q > 0"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle q>0}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>q</mi>
        <mo>></mo>
        <mn>0</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle q>0}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/482e0a33d9e8fd6307b5f68a5182c2d0d14efc9c" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:5.33ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle q>0}"/></span>, don't vary holomorphically. But, the filtrations can vary holomorphically, giving a better defined structure.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwTA" aria-labelledby="Morphisms_of_mixed_Hodge_structures"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Morphisms_of_mixed_Hodge_structures">Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><p id="mwTQ">
Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are defined by maps of abelian groups</p><blockquote id="mwTg"><p id="mwTw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt32" id="mwUA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"f:(H_\\mathbb{Z},W_\\bullet, F^\\bullet) \\to (H_\\mathbb{Z}&apos;,W_\\bullet&apos;, F&apos;^\\bullet)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle f:(H_{\mathbb {Z} },W_{\bullet },F^{\bullet })\to (H_{\mathbb {Z} }',W_{\bullet }',F'^{\bullet })}">
