</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwWg" aria-labelledby="Further_definitions_and_properties"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Further_definitions_and_properties">Further definitions and properties</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Further definitions and properties"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwWw" aria-labelledby="Hodge_numbers"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Hodge_numbers">Hodge numbers</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Hodge numbers"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><p id="mwXA">
The Hodge numbers of a MHS are defined as the dimensions</p><blockquote id="mwXQ"><p id="mwXg"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt36" id="mwXw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"h^{p,q}(H_\\mathbb{Z}) = \\dim_\\mathbb{C}\\text{Gr}_{F^\\bullet}^p\\text{Gr}_{p+q}^{W_\\bullet}H_\\mathbb{C} "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle h^{p,q}(H_{\mathbb {Z} })=\dim _{\mathbb {C} }{\text{Gr}}_{F^{\bullet }}^{p}{\text{Gr}}_{p+q}^{W_{\bullet }}H_{\mathbb {C} }}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
