</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ed9d3b43fb0e3ee4b9bc392664cf5bd18981d96e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.889ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (p+q)}"/></span> Hodge structure.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwaQ" aria-labelledby="Homological_properties"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Homological_properties">Homological properties</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Homological properties"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><p id="mwag">
There is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abelian_category" title="Abelian category" id="mwaw">Abelian category</a><sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-2" id="mwbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">]</span></span></a></sup> of mixed Hodge structures which has vanishing <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt43" id="mwcA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\text{Ext}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\text{Ext}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mtext>Ext</mtext>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\text{Ext}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3fbe87fd94b9aa18833d92e77eacadf32dd17da4" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:3.715ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\text{Ext}}}"/></span>-groups whenever the cohomological degree is greater than <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt44" id="mwcQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 1}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mn>1</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle 1}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/92d98b82a3778f043108d4e20960a9193df57cbf" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.162ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 1}"/></span>: that is, given mixed hodge structures <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt45" id="mwcg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(H_\\mathbb{Z},W_\\bullet, F^\\bullet), (H_\\mathbb{Z}&apos;,W_\\bullet&apos;, F&apos;^\\bullet)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (H_{\mathbb {Z} },W_{\bullet },F^{\bullet }),(H_{\mathbb {Z} }',W_{\bullet }',F'^{\bullet })}">
