</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwfQ" aria-labelledby="Mixed_Hodge_structures_on_bi-filtered_complexes"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Mixed_Hodge_structures_on_bi-filtered_complexes">Mixed Hodge structures on bi-filtered complexes</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Mixed Hodge structures on bi-filtered complexes"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><p id="mwfg">
Many mixed Hodge structures can be constructed from a bifiltered complex. This includes complements of smooth varieties defined by the complement of a normal crossing variety. Given a complex of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheaf_of_abelian_groups" title="Sheaf of abelian groups" class="mw-redirect" id="mwfw">sheaves of abelian groups</a> <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt52" id="mwgA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"A^\\bullet"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle A^{\bullet }}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>A</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∙<!-- ∙ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle A^{\bullet }}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1640b7dd4c74020944918838bac76fa9c9fac0d3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.797ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle A^{\bullet }}"/></span> and filtrations <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt53" id="mwgQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"W_\\bullet, F^\\bullet"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle W_{\bullet },F^{\bullet }}">
