</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/76d2981dd2f37bec74de35e5706f431625648def" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -2.303ex; margin-bottom: -0.202ex; width:18.457ex; height:6.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\begin{aligned}d(W_{i}A^{\bullet })&amp;\subset W_{i}A^{\bullet }\\d(F^{i}A^{\bullet })&amp;\subset F^{i}A^{\bullet }\end{aligned}}}"/></span></p></blockquote><p id="mwiQ">There is an induced mixed Hodge structure on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperhomology" title="Hyperhomology" id="mwig">hyperhomology</a> groups</p><blockquote id="mwiw"><p id="mwjA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt56" id="mwjQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(\\mathbb{H}^k(X,A^\\bullet), W_\\bullet, F^\\bullet)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (\mathbb {H} ^{k}(X,A^{\bullet }),W_{\bullet },F^{\bullet })}">
