    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\begin{aligned}W_{m}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;={\begin{cases}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;{\text{ if }}i\leq m\\\Omega _{X}^{i-m}\wedge \Omega _{X}^{m}(\log D)&amp;{\text{ if }}0\leq m\leq i\\0&amp;{\text{ if }}m&lt;0\end{cases}}\\[6pt]F^{p}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;={\begin{cases}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;{\text{ if }}p\leq i\\0&amp;{\text{ otherwise}}\end{cases}}\end{aligned}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/29c06302ad297443b9f5441450b7cf5dffaf4d6e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -7.838ex; width:54.211ex; height:16.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\begin{aligned}W_{m}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;={\begin{cases}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;{\text{ if }}i\leq m\\\Omega _{X}^{i-m}\wedge \Omega _{X}^{m}(\log D)&amp;{\text{ if }}0\leq m\leq i\\0&amp;{\text{ if }}m&lt;0\end{cases}}\\[6pt]F^{p}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;={\begin{cases}\Omega _{X}^{i}(\log D)&amp;{\text{ if }}p\leq i\\0&amp;{\text{ otherwise}}\end{cases}}\end{aligned}}}"/></span></p></blockquote><p id="mwoA">It turns out these filtrations define a natural mixed Hodge structure on the cohomology group <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt63" id="mwoQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^n(U,\\mathbb{C})"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{n}(U,\mathbb {C} )}">
