</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mw0Q" aria-labelledby="Examples"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Examples">Examples</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Examples"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mw0g" aria-labelledby="Complement_of_a_smooth_projective_curve_by_two_points"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Complement_of_a_smooth_projective_curve_by_two_points">Complement of a smooth projective curve by two points</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Mixed_Hodge_structure&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Complement of a smooth projective curve by two points"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mw0w">We give here the simplest example which isolates the phenomenon at hand. We will explain the MHS on (a twist of) <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt87" id="mw1A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^1(U,\\mathbb{Z})"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{1}(U,\mathbb {Z} )}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>U</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{1}(U,\mathbb {Z} )}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7cdf03936274cfe012c022c2ba1ebf856eb23d52" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:9.334ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{1}(U,\mathbb {Z} )}"/></span> where <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt88" id="mw1Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"U"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle U}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>U</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle U}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/458a728f53b9a0274f059cd695e067c430956025" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.783ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle U}"/></span> is the complement of a smooth projective curve by two points.</p><p id="mw1g">

Let <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt89" id="mw1w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span> be a smooth proper (hence projective) curve over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt90" id="mw2A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":" \\mathbb{C} "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {C} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">C</mi>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {C} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f9add4085095b9b6d28d045fd9c92c2c09f549a7" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.678ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {C} }"/></span> and let <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt91" id="mw2Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"Z:=\\{x,y\\}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle Z:=\{x,y\}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>Z</mi>
        <mo>:=</mo>
        <mo fence="false" stretchy="false">{</mo>
        <mi>x</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>y</mi>
        <mo fence="false" stretchy="false">}</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle Z:=\{x,y\}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/0f3d0f207162146a1f9bdd8201f3808c6a57dbe9" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:11.27ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle Z:=\{x,y\}}"/></span> be two points in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt92" id="mw2g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span>. We get a so called recollement situation </p><blockquote id="mw2w">  <p id="mw3A"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt93" id="mw3Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"i:Z\\hookrightarrow X \\hookleftarrow U:j "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle i:Z\hookrightarrow X\hookleftarrow U:j}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>i</mi>
        <mo>:</mo>
        <mi>Z</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">↪<!-- ↪ --></mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">↩<!-- ↩ --></mo>
        <mi>U</mi>
        <mo>:</mo>
        <mi>j</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle i:Z\hookrightarrow X\hookleftarrow U:j}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c6112394dc06ddea4b1e05177079b8f4f4907329" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:18.891ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle i:Z\hookrightarrow X\hookleftarrow U:j}"/></span></p></blockquote><p id="mw3g"> where <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt94" id="mw3w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"U:=X-Z"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle U:=X-Z}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>U</mi>
        <mo>:=</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
        <mi>Z</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle U:=X-Z}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/51e635869e8adde7f6e7a494c23c852313865dce" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.505ex; width:12.029ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle U:=X-Z}"/></span>. </p>

<p id="mw4A">One has an exact triangle of constructible sheaves on <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt95" id="mw4Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span></p>  

<blockquote id="mw4g"><p id="mw4w"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt96" id="mw5A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"i_*i^!\\mathbb{Z}_X\\to \\mathbb{Z}_X\\to Rj_*j^*\\mathbb{Z}_X\\xrightarrow{+} "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle i_{*}i^{!}\mathbb {Z} _{X}\to \mathbb {Z} _{X}\to Rj_{*}j^{*}\mathbb {Z} _{X}\xrightarrow {+} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>i</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <msup>
          <mi>i</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>!</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>R</mi>
        <msub>
          <mi>j</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
