  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/2cc90d4b87a036d5ca83019a190e0b6729aaf58c" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:62.803ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 0\to H^{1}(X,\mathbb {Z} )\to H^{1}(U,\mathbb {Z} )\to H^{0}(Z,\mathbb {Z} )(-1)\to H^{2}(X,\mathbb {Z} )\to 0}"/></span> </p></blockquote>
<p id="mw7A">
<br id="mw7Q"/>
Rationalizing, and noting that <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt99" id="mw7g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^2(X,\\mathbb{Q})=\\mathbb{Q}(-1)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{2}(X,\mathbb {Q} )=\mathbb {Q} (-1)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Q</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{2}(X,\mathbb {Q} )=\mathbb {Q} (-1)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/2616a0327ea465805fca101fed1aedd468a7207c" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:19.476ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{2}(X,\mathbb {Q} )=\mathbb {Q} (-1)}"/></span>, we get a sequence of rational MHS</p>

<blockquote id="mw7w"><p id="mw8A"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt100" id="mw8Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"0\\to H^1(X,\\mathbb{Q})(1)\\to  H^1(U,\\mathbb{Q})(1)\\to \\mathbb{Q} \\to  0 "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 0\to H^{1}(X,\mathbb {Q} )(1)\to H^{1}(U,\mathbb {Q} )(1)\to \mathbb {Q} \to 0}">
  <semantics>
