    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle i_{*}i^{!}\mathbb {Z} _{X}\to \mathbb {Z} _{X}\to \mathbf {R} j_{*}\mathbb {Z} _{U}\xrightarrow {[+1]} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9bbda8e74aa93d4c01b80258deb3cb8974f5ed46" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; margin-top: -0.346ex; width:28.985ex; height:4.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle i_{*}i^{!}\mathbb {Z} _{X}\to \mathbb {Z} _{X}\to \mathbf {R} j_{*}\mathbb {Z} _{U}\xrightarrow {[+1]} }"/></span></p></blockquote><p id="mwARw">whenever <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt124" id="mwAR0" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span> is smooth. Note the homology groups <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt125" id="mwAR4" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{BM}_k(X)  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3e71cb25418de1cce5df9dab282928e2574d2d51" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:9.099ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(X)}"/></span> are called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borel–Moore_homology" title="Borel–Moore homology" id="mwAR8">Borel–Moore homology</a>, which are dual to cohomology for general spaces and the <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt126" id="mwASA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(n)  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (n)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle (n)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6dcf3083121187f661e0add2f50615aa21428e68" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:3.204ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (n)}"/></span> means tensoring with the Tate structure <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt127" id="mwASE" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{Z}(1)^{\\otimes n}  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Z} (1)^{\otimes n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <msup>
          <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>⊗<!-- ⊗ --></mo>
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {Z} (1)^{\otimes n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/52ed83425a39a13efbcf9f5ab7b53b13d71fc702" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:7.019ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Z} (1)^{\otimes n}}"/></span> add weight <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt128" id="mwASI" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"-2n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle -2n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
        <mn>2</mn>
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle -2n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d79eeae817589c40825c8ec9e4a3017e57185a2d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.505ex; width:4.365ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle -2n}"/></span> to the weight filtration. The smoothness hypothesis is required because <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdier_duality" title="Verdier duality" id="mwASM">Verdier duality</a> implies <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt129" id="mwASQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"i^!D_X = D_Y  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle i^{!}D_{X}=D_{Y}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>i</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>!</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <msub>
          <mi>D</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>D</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>Y</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle i^{!}D_{X}=D_{Y}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9b09c3ae13c5903b1b660d0435506f4b370ac370" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:11.558ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle i^{!}D_{X}=D_{Y}}"/></span>, and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt130" id="mwASU" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"D_X \\cong \\mathbb{Z}_X[2n]  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle D_{X}\cong \mathbb {Z} _{X}[2n]}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>D</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>≅<!-- ≅ --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mn>2</mn>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle D_{X}\cong \mathbb {Z} _{X}[2n]}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ec365f77c97ba826e927cb6685ddcb80fc77114b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:13.689ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle D_{X}\cong \mathbb {Z} _{X}[2n]}"/></span> whenever <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt131" id="mwASY" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span> is smooth. Also, the dualizing complex for <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt132" id="mwASc" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span> has weight <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt133" id="mwASg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"n  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a601995d55609f2d9f5e233e36fbe9ea26011b3b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.395ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n}"/></span>, hence <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt134" id="mwASk" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"D_X \\cong \\mathbb{Z}_X[2n](n)  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle D_{X}\cong \mathbb {Z} _{X}[2n](n)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>D</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>≅<!-- ≅ --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mn>2</mn>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle D_{X}\cong \mathbb {Z} _{X}[2n](n)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a4a9bc8d974873a923eb97534186f17ee724c241" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:16.893ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle D_{X}\cong \mathbb {Z} _{X}[2n](n)}"/></span>. Also, the maps from Borel-Moore homology must be twisted by up to weight <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt135" id="mwASo" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(n)  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (n)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle (n)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6dcf3083121187f661e0add2f50615aa21428e68" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:3.204ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (n)}"/></span> is order for it to have a map to <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt136" id="mwASs" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^m(X)  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{m}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>m</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{m}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/577498cec194c33d0f096ce66d8bffee8323a44b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:7.568ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{m}(X)}"/></span>. Also, there is the perfect duality pairing</p><blockquote id="mwASw"><p id="mwAS0"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt137" id="mwAS4" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{BM}_{2n-m}(Y)\\times H^m(Y) \\to \\mathbb{Z}  "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{2n-m}^{BM}(Y)\times H^{m}(Y)\to \mathbb {Z} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
